<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 187 0 R
/T (This report presents the implementation and outcomes of a Hot Meal Distribution Program conducted in Sadiqabad, District Rahim Yar Khan, Punjab, Pakistan. The initiative was funded by Arrahman Welfare Foundation Canada \(AWFCA\) and implemented in collaboration with the on ground partner Arrahman Welfare Foundation. The hot meal distribution was organized to provide freshly prepared, nutritious meals to poor and needy families who deserved support and were experiencing financial hardship. The program aimed to reduce food insecurity by ensuring that vulnerable community members had access to healthy meals served with dignity and compassion. The initiative benefited 150 families, representing approximately 350 individuals, through the distribution of freshly prepared hot meals. The program contributed to improving food security while strengthening community well-being and providing immediate relief to those most in need.)
/E (This report presents the implementation and outcomes of a Hot Meal Distribution Program conducted in Sadiqabad, District Rahim Yar Khan, Punjab, Pakistan. The initiative was funded by Arrahman Welfare Foundation Canada \(AWFCA\) and implemented in collaboration with the on ground partner Arrahman Welfare Foundation. The hot meal distribution was organized to provide freshly prepared, nutritious meals to poor and needy families who deserved support and were experiencing financial hardship. The program aimed to reduce food insecurity by ensuring that vulnerable community members had access to healthy meals served with dignity and compassion. The initiative benefited 150 families, representing approximately 350 individuals, through the distribution of freshly prepared hot meals. The program contributed to improving food security while strengthening community well-being and providing immediate relief to those most in need.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
